server: make llama_server() embeddable in a host process (no signal handlers, stoppable)

b9870 exposes int llama_server(int, char **) with no main() in server.cpp; this patch adds what a
JVM host needs to run it inside libjllama: a g_llama_server_embedded flag with
llama_server_set_embedded() / llama_server_request_shutdown() (declared by the host in
native_server_bridge.h), no process-wide SIGINT/SIGTERM handlers in embedded mode (they would
hijack the JVM's), and a shutdown handler guarded by g_shutdown_handler_mutex and reset before the
locals it captures are destroyed -- a request landing after llama_server() returned used to run the
lambda over destroyed objects (SIGSEGV in server_http_context::stop(), seen in router mode).
Runnable guard: src/test/cpp/test_native_server_shutdown.cpp.

Refreshed at b11881: #31113 split llama_server() into one function per role (server_run_router,
server_run_instance, server_run_download) and added server_run_opts. The embedded mode now clears
server_run_opts::install_signal_handlers (upstream's own switch, which llama-cli uses) instead of
guarding the sigaction block, and each role function that installs a shutdown handler declares the
reset after the last local its handler captures: models_routes in the router, ctx_http in the
instance.

Refreshed at b12014: #31417 removed the Windows argv reconstruction from common_params_parse (the
defect 0001 carried a fix for, dropped at the same bump), so the forwarded-argv hunk is gone:
llama_server() calls common_params_parse for every caller, and it parses the argv it is given.

Refreshed at b12316: #31467 made the download progress throttle per file and added
`#include <mutex>` (and <unordered_map>) to server.cpp itself, so the hunk that added the include
for g_shutdown_handler_mutex is gone. 6 hunks: the flag, the guarded handler, the two resets, and
opts.install_signal_handlers.

Since the review of 2026-11-18 the embedded server also skips the common_log_flush() at the end of
llama_server(): it pauses and resumes common_log's worker without the engine's g_common_log_mutex,
and the host's setLogger / log-file changes take that lock.

Since round three of that review the patch also adds llama_server_parsed(params, argc, argv): the
same server over an argv the embedding host has parsed already. NativeServer's engine parses the
argv once, under its log lock, to refuse a bad argv at the start and to own the log file; a second
parse inside llama_server() read every file option again, and one from a pipe (--api-key-file
/dev/stdin) the second time empty -- the server then ran without its API key. llama_server_parsed()
does not call common_init(): the host calls it before its parse, as llama_server() does, since
2026-11-19 -- called after the parse it turned common_log's prefix and timestamps on again, so
--no-log-prefix / --no-log-timestamps had no effect (CApiLogFile.TheLogPrefixAndTimestampOptionsOfTheArgvTakeEffect).

Drop-check on every bump: none of this is upstream's yet. Read tools/server/server.cpp for an
embedded mode of its own (no process signal handlers, an out-of-band shutdown, a parse the caller
does) -- once it has one, port native_server.cpp to it and drop the patch.

diff --git a/tools/server/server.cpp b/tools/server/server.cpp
index d14978286..97ad17901 100644
--- a/tools/server/server.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server.cpp
@@ -29,6 +29,53 @@
 static std::function<void(int)> shutdown_handler;
 static std::atomic_flag is_terminating = ATOMIC_FLAG_INIT;
 
+// [jllama] Embedded-mode support: when llama_server() is hosted inside libjllama and driven over
+// JNI (net.ladenthin.llama.server.NativeServer), it must NOT install process-wide signal handlers
+// (that would hijack the JVM's SIGINT/SIGTERM), and it must be stoppable out-of-band because
+// ctx_server is local to the role function. The forwarded argv needs no special case any more:
+// since b12014 (#31417) common_params_parse parses exactly the argv it is given on every platform.
+// These symbols are declared in src/main/cpp/native_server_bridge.h and called by
+// native_server.cpp.
+static std::atomic<bool> g_llama_server_embedded{false};
+
+void llama_server_set_embedded(bool embedded) {
+    g_llama_server_embedded.store(embedded);
+}
+
+// [jllama] shutdown_handler captures the role function's locals by reference and upstream never
+// clears it, so a request that lands after llama_server() returned ran it over destroyed objects
+// (SIGSEGV in server_http_context::stop(), seen in RouterModeIntegrationTest's tearDown). The JNI
+// caller signals repeatedly until the server has returned, so that window is routinely hit. Two
+// guards close it: every write of the handler and every invocation from another thread holds this
+// mutex, and a llama_server_shutdown_handler_reset declared after the captured locals clears the
+// handler before any of them is destroyed. The handler is invoked under the lock, so the reset --
+// and therefore the destruction of what it captures -- waits for an invocation in progress.
+static std::mutex g_shutdown_handler_mutex;
+
+static void llama_server_set_shutdown_handler(std::function<void(int)> handler) {
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(g_shutdown_handler_mutex);
+    shutdown_handler = std::move(handler);
+}
+
+struct llama_server_shutdown_handler_reset {
+    llama_server_shutdown_handler_reset() = default;
+    llama_server_shutdown_handler_reset(const llama_server_shutdown_handler_reset &) = delete;
+    llama_server_shutdown_handler_reset & operator=(const llama_server_shutdown_handler_reset &) = delete;
+    ~llama_server_shutdown_handler_reset() {
+        llama_server_set_shutdown_handler(nullptr);
+    }
+};
+
+void llama_server_request_shutdown() {
+    // Mirrors the SIGTERM path: invoke the installed shutdown_handler, which unblocks
+    // ctx_server.start_loop() (instance) / ctx_http.stop() (router). No-op if the server has not
+    // finished starting (handler not yet installed) or has already returned (handler reset).
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(g_shutdown_handler_mutex);
+    if (shutdown_handler) {
+        shutdown_handler(SIGTERM);
+    }
+}
+
 static inline void signal_handler(int signal) {
     if (is_terminating.test_and_set()) {
         // in case it hangs, we can force terminate the server by hitting Ctrl+C twice
@@ -48,6 +95,8 @@ struct server_run_opts {
 
 // satisfies -Wmissing-declarations (used by llama command)
 int llama_server(int argc, char ** argv);
+// [jllama] llama_server() over an argv the embedding host has parsed already (see below)
+int llama_server_parsed(common_params & params, int argc, char ** argv);
 
 // to be used via CLI (argc / argv are used by router mode only)
 int llama_server(common_params & params, int argc, char ** argv);
@@ -511,6 +560,9 @@ static int server_run_router(common_params & params, int argc, char ** argv, con
 
     // setup server instances manager
     std::optional<server_models_routes> models_routes;
+    // [jllama] declared after every local the shutdown handler captures (models_routes, ctx_http,
+    // mcp_mgr), so it clears the handler before any of them is destroyed
+    llama_server_shutdown_handler_reset shutdown_handler_reset;
     try {
         models_routes.emplace(params, argc, argv);
     } catch (const std::exception & e) {
@@ -587,14 +639,14 @@ static int server_run_router(common_params & params, int argc, char ** argv, con
     }
     ctx_http.is_ready.store(true);
 
-    shutdown_handler = [&](int) {
+    llama_server_set_shutdown_handler([&](int) {
         if (models_routes.has_value()) {
             // important to disconnect any SSE clients
             models_routes->stopping.store(true);
         }
         mcp_mgr.shutdown();
         ctx_http.stop();
-    };
+    });
 
     try {
         models_routes->models.load_startup_models();
@@ -655,6 +707,9 @@ static int server_run_instance(common_params & params, server_role & role, commo
     server_tools   tools;
 
     server_http_context ctx_http;
+    // [jllama] declared after every local the shutdown handler captures (ctx_server, mcp_mgr), so
+    // it clears the handler before any of them is destroyed
+    llama_server_shutdown_handler_reset shutdown_handler_reset;
     if (!ctx_http.init(params)) {
         SRV_ERR("%s", "failed to initialize HTTP server\n");
         return 1;
@@ -707,11 +762,11 @@ static int server_run_instance(common_params & params, server_role & role, commo
 
     SRV_INF("%s", "model loaded\n");
 
-    shutdown_handler = [&](int) {
+    llama_server_set_shutdown_handler([&](int) {
         mcp_mgr.shutdown();
         // this will unblock start_loop()
         ctx_server.terminate();
-    };
+    });
 
     if (opts.install_signal_handlers) {
         server_install_signal_handlers();
@@ -823,8 +878,49 @@ int llama_server(int argc, char ** argv) {
     llama_backend_init();
     llama_numa_init(params.numa);
 
-    const int result = server_run(params, argc, argv, role, server_run_opts{});
-    common_log_flush(common_log_main());
+    server_run_opts opts;
+    // [jllama] no process-wide SIGINT/SIGTERM handlers when embedded in the JVM (they would hijack
+    // the JVM's own); NativeServer stops the embedded server via llama_server_request_shutdown()
+    opts.install_signal_handlers = !g_llama_server_embedded.load();
+    const int result = server_run(params, argc, argv, role, opts);
+    // [jllama] embedded, the host owns common_log and changes it under a lock of its own: this flush
+    // (a pause and a resume of the log worker) raced a setLogger on another thread, and the worker
+    // writes what is queued without it
+    if (!g_llama_server_embedded.load()) {
+        common_log_flush(common_log_main());
+    }
+    return result;
+}
+
+// [jllama] llama_server() for an embedding host that parsed the argv itself, once (NativeServer's
+// engine parses it before the worker starts, under its own lock, to refuse a bad argv at the start
+// and to own the log file): a second parse here read every file option again, and one from a pipe
+// (--api-key-file /dev/stdin) the second time empty -- a server without its API key. argv is still
+// what router mode hands its workers.
+int llama_server_parsed(common_params & params, int argc, char ** argv) {
+    server_role role;
+
+    std::setlocale(LC_NUMERIC, "C");
+
+#ifndef _WIN32
+    signal(SIGPIPE, SIG_IGN);
+#endif
+
+    // the host called common_init() before its parse (prepare_server_argv), as llama_server() does: here
+    // it would turn on again the log prefix and timestamps the argv turned off
+    server_stream_session_manager_start();
+
+    SRV_INF("%s", "initializing ...\n");
+
+    llama_backend_init();
+    llama_numa_init(params.numa);
+
+    server_run_opts opts;
+    opts.install_signal_handlers = !g_llama_server_embedded.load();
+    const int result = server_run(params, argc, argv, role, opts);
+    if (!g_llama_server_embedded.load()) {
+        common_log_flush(common_log_main());
+    }
     return result;
 }
 
